      "kind": "lede",
      "html": "<p>A security system is only as good as its last honest inspection. A camera knocked off its view. A door that no longer fails safe. A sign blown off. None of them announce themselves. They show up after an incident, when the footage was never recorded.</p>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "takeaways",
      "heading": "The short version",
      "html": "<ul><li>One walk covers three systems: CCTV, access control and intruder alarm.</li><li>CCTV that records identifiable people handles personal data under UK GDPR. Signs, lawful reason and retention are part of the check.</li><li>The Surveillance Camera Code of Practice (England and Wales) places a duty to have regard on public bodies such as local authorities and police.</li><li>Door fail states must match the fire evacuation design.</li><li>A photo taken on the spot beats a note typed later.</li><li>Quickler records the walk and writes the report. It does not decide compliance. You do.</li></ul>"
