      "heading": "Questions, answered",
      "html": "<h3>What does a CCTV and access control inspection cover?</h3><p>One walk, three systems. CCTV: do the cameras work, cover the right area, record and keep footage, and show privacy signs. Access control: do readers work, and do doors lock and release as designed. Intruder alarm: do zones and tamper work, and does the alarm reach someone. Quickler keeps a photo for each.</p><h3>Is a CCTV inspection a data protection matter?</h3><p>Partly. A camera that records identifiable people handles personal data under UK GDPR and the Data Protection Act 2018. So signs, a lawful reason and a retention period matter. The Information Commission publishes video surveillance guidance. Quickler keeps the sign photo and the retention setting. Whether your use is lawful is for your data protection officer.</p><h3>What is fail-safe and fail-secure?</h3><p>Fail-safe: the door unlocks when power fails, so people can get out. Fail-secure: the door stays locked to protect a secure area. The right one follows the fire and security design. You record what you saw.</p><h3>Can I do a security inspection in WhatsApp?</h3><p>Yes. You get each question in your usual chat. Answer by text, voice note or photo of the camera view or reader. Quickler writes the report. No new app. No login.</p><h3>Related guides</h3><ul><li><a href=\"/pages/it-asset-audit-app-uk.html\">IT asset audit app</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/data-centre-audit-software-uk.html\">Data centre audit software</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/iso-27001-physical-security-audit-uk.html\">ISO 27001 physical security audit</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/comms-room-inspection-checklist-uk.html\">Comms room inspection checklist</a></li></ul>"
